{{also|Folgen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|volgen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|folgēn}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*folgēn}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*fulgāną}}. {{doublet|de|followen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈfɔlɡŋ̩/|/ˈfɔlɡən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-folgen.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|<sein>}} {{tlb|de|intransitive}}

# to [[follow]] {{q|on the same path or in a sequence}} {{+obj|de|dat<someone>}}
#: {{uxa|de|Der Held '''folgte''' dem Drachen zu seiner Höhle.|The hero '''followed''' the dragon to its cave.}}
#: {{uxa|de|Drei Jahre später '''folgte''' eine Fortsetzung des ersten Films.|Three years later a sequel '''followed''' the first film.}}
# to [[understand]], to be [[attentive]] to {{+obj|de|dat<something, e.g. a book, film plot, etc.>}}
#: {{uxa|de|Ich konnte der Handlung des Films nicht '''folgen'''.|I couldn't '''follow''' the plot of the film.}}
# to [[follow]] {{q|as a consequence}}, to [[result]] {{+obj|de|:aus(dat)<from something>}}
#: {{uxa|de|Daraus '''folgt''', dass der Butler es getan hat.|It '''follows''' that the butler did it.}}
# to [[obey]], to [[follow]], to [[accede]], to [[comply]] with {{+obj|de|dat<instructions, advice, a request, rules, the law, etc.>}}
#: {{uxa|de|Ich habe entschieden, Ihrem Rat zu '''folgen'''.|I've decided to '''follow''' your advice.}}
#: {{uxa|de|Das Gericht ist dem Antrag nicht '''gefolgt'''.|The court has not '''acceded''' to the request.}}
# {{lb|de|social media}} to [[follow]] {{gloss|to subscribe to see content from an account on a social media platform}} {{+obj|de|dat<someone, an account, etc.>}}
#: {{syn|de|followen}}

